      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting `this.threads \u003d []` when `hidden` is true unmounts all `\u003cgr-comment-thread\u003e` elements from the DOM. If a user is in the middle of drafting a comment in standard diff mode and clicks \"Rich diff\", `\u003cgr-comment\u003e` is unmounted immediately. Because draft auto-saving is debounced (`AUTO_SAVE_DEBOUNCE_DELAY_MS`) and `disconnectedCallback` does not flush pending edits, any unsaved draft content in local component state will be lost without warning.\n\nAdditionally, `hidden` is a generic reflected HTML attribute on `GrDiffHost`, so any other visibility toggles (collapse, tabs, modals) will also tear down comment threads.\n\nConsider ensuring in-flight drafts are flushed/saved before unmounting threads (or before toggling views), or using a more scoped property / inert handling rather than clearing `threads` directly on `hidden`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "9a0ae3cbf660d38c125b1f9a7f7eaf41d29ea689",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
