      "writtenOn": "2026-09-04T19:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing this block introduces a few subtle regressions:\n\n1. **Divergent thread computation**: `gr-diff-view` now computes `threadsForFile` via a getter for `\u003cgr-diff-markdown-viewer\u003e`, while `\u003cgr-diff-host\u003e` independently computes threads in its own `willUpdate`. This duplicates the logic for resolving file threads and `old_path` mappings.\n2. **Missing reactive triggers**: The removed block explicitly triggered on changes to `files`, `change`, `path`, `patchNum`, and `basePatchNum`. If `files` loads asynchronously after `diffHost` has initialized (e.g. populating `old_path` for renamed files), `diffHost` may not re-trigger thread computation.\n3. **Timing guarantee lost**: The previous `this.diffHost.updateComplete.then(...)` ensured that the diff DOM structure and slots were ready before comment threads were slotted into the diff table.\n\nIt seems this was removed because the async `then()` callback was overwriting `diffHost.threads \u003d []` when hidden. Instead of removing parent coordination and having `gr-diff-host` inspect its own `hidden` property, consider keeping thread coordination in `gr-diff-view` and conditionally passing/setting threads only when rich markdown view is inactive (e.g. `if (!this.isShowingRichMarkdown())`).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "9a0ae3cbf660d38c125b1f9a7f7eaf41d29ea689",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
